WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.683
- This looks good to me.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.987
I was gonna say don't put your face in it

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:08.466
and I just put my face in it.

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:10.407
(breathes deeply)
(exhales sharply)

00:00:10.407 --> 00:00:12.990
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.600
Hey, what's up? It's Tway.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.850
And welcome to "Making It Big".

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.530
The show where my friends challenge me

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.470
to make their favorite foods big.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.500
So, you might notice that my
table here is a little warped

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.740
and that's because we're
filming everything in VR.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.480
You can watch the full VR episode

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.150
with a Meta Quest 2 in Mega Tasty.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.530
That's our virtual cooking world

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.980
within Horizon Worlds,
or on Meta Quest TV.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.620
Today, I have a very special guest.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.173
It's Miss Asia Jackson.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.170
Hi, welcome to the show.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.420
- Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.380
- How are you today?

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.250
- I'm good, how are you?

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.200
- I am kind of nervous right now.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.070
- Kind of nervous?

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.630
- Yeah.
- [Asia] As you should.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.960
- I just don't know what
you're gonna challenge me to,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.750
and I feel like you are very particular.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.040
- Yes.
- So I really have

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.435
to nail this.
- Yes, you do.

00:01:06.435 --> 00:01:08.250
- [Tway] Whatever this is.
- Absolutely, yeah.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.780
- So, let's see it.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.163
- All right. Here we go.

00:01:12.075 --> 00:01:12.988
Ta-da.

00:01:12.988 --> 00:01:14.850
- [Tway] Oh, wow.
- [Asia] Yes.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.110
- [Tway] Vietnamese egg rolls.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.550
- [Asia] Vietnamese egg rolls.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.383
Look at that.

00:01:18.383 --> 00:01:21.840
- Okay. So explain to me
why Vietnamese egg rolls.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.680
- So I'm half Filipino, we
have our own egg roll version.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:27.240
- Yeah.
- We call it lumpia.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.710
But it's such a staple in
East and Southeast Asia,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.200
so I was like, let's have
her show us how to make

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.056
a gigantic Vietnamese egg roll.

00:01:37.056 --> 00:01:38.660
- Wow. What about sauce?

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.440
Do you want a dipping sauce on the side?

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.273
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:44.700
- Okay. I actually have
a special sauce I make

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.140
for my egg rolls.
- Ooh.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.850
- So if you don't mind,
I can make that for you.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.810
- Yeah, I'd love to try it.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.720
- I have a lot of work to do.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.800
I will see you later.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.210
- All right, girl.
- [Tway] Thanks, friend.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:55.473
- I put my trust to you.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.353
- Let's get to it.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.470
First things first, the wrapper.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.910
When I make egg rolls,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.790
I usually just use the
wrapper from the store,

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:12.750
but we couldn't find
any that was big enough.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.150
So I have my flour here.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.150
I am going to add in some salt.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.890
I'm adding hot water just
so it can hydrate the dough.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.600
There has been some debate between

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.630
if this is an egg roll or a spring roll.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:28.590
But you know what?

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:31.440
To me, this is cha gio.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.183
That means egg roll in
Vietnamese. (chuckles)

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.286
I love playing with dough.

00:02:39.286 --> 00:02:42.210
(upbeat music)

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:46.323
Put this in my bowl and
let it rest for 30 minutes.

00:02:47.179 --> 00:02:49.762
(upbeat music)

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.790
So the reason why I
needed this dough to rest

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:58.590
is because I need the gluten
to just calm down a little bit

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.350
or else I won't be able to spread them out

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.453
as thin as I would like to.

00:03:06.243 --> 00:03:08.826
(upbeat music)

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.740
I think this is the perfect
thickness for the egg roll too.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:17.940
So, yeah.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.940
I am going to let this
wrapper rest in the fridge

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.040
just so when I fill it
up with the filling,

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.350
it can stay the shape.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.183
See you later.

00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:33.291
(upbeat music)

00:03:34.609 --> 00:03:36.172
(bowl clanking)

00:03:36.172 --> 00:03:39.900
(meditation chants)

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.250
So now, I'm going to
combine my minced pork,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.980
the shrimps, the onions.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.830
See all this different
texture that's going in

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.650
is really going to give
it a nice mouth feel

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.850
when you bite into it.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:58.233
The carrots, the noodles, the mushrooms.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:03.120
Egg yolks hence egg rolls.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.470
Green onions.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.330
Minced garlic.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.180
And there's already a
lot of flavors in here,

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.550
but we do need to add seasoning

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.070
because you need to season your food.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.183
Sesame oil.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:19.950
Just a little bit because
this is really over powering.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:24.677
My favorite thing in the whole
entire world, fish sauce.

00:04:24.677 --> 00:04:25.770
(speaks in Vietnamese)

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.270
It's a replacement for salt,

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:31.590
but it also adds that like
nice umami touch to it

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.690
when you bite into something

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.370
that's been seasoned with fish sauce.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.410
You know that it's not just
been seasoned with salt.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.023
It's been seasoned with love.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.470
So we have sugar here.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:44.373
Pepper.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.880
Are you ready? 'Cause I am.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.620
Whoa.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.580
Nice massage.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.343
Don't you wish you can
just get in here with me?

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.470
Here you go.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.150
This is our filling.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.067
(triumphant music)

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.700
I've rolled many egg rolls in my life.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.820
I have never rolled one this big.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.773
Let's do this.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.043
Oop.

00:05:16.043 --> 00:05:19.100
(bright upbeat music)

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.320
Let's close.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.930
Everything is nice and tight.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.453
I have my egg wash here.

00:05:27.453 --> 00:05:29.940
(upbeat music)

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.323
Fold it over.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.700
All right.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.659
I think I'm ready.

00:05:37.659 --> 00:05:40.659
(suspenseful music)

00:05:42.682 --> 00:05:43.515
Yes.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.053
Wow.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:54.393
And this is my giant egg roll.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.310
I hope that you cook all the way through.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:01.083
If you don't, you are a disappointment.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.360
Let's get this in the fryer.

00:06:06.735 --> 00:06:10.080
(upbeat music)

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.880
Welcome to the back kitchen.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.400
So I have my cha gio here.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.200
The fryer is over there.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.020
As you can see, the
friendly fry guy is here.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.640
- [Voiceover] Fry guy.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.893
Your guy to anything fry.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.210
- I am going to stay
my butt right over here

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.930
because that's 10 gallons of hot oil

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.570
that I'm kinda scared of.

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:35.820
So I'm gonna hand this over to you.

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.593
Drop that egg roll.

00:06:38.866 --> 00:06:41.366
(oil sizzles)

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.430
All right.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.740
I'll see you in two hours.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:50.583
Bye, friend.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.115
(upbeat music)

00:06:55.115 --> 00:06:57.420
So my baby is in the fryer.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.150
So that gives me time to make the sauce.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:04.140
Usually, I like to eat my
egg rolls with Mae Ploy,

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.490
a sweet chili sauce.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:09.090
But this is my recipe, so
we'll call it Tway Ploy.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.280
I have some Fresno chilies here

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.520
that I'm just going to give a rough chop.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.460
And then I have some
Thai chilies over here,

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.260
Bird's eye chilies.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.930
Okay. I have my garlic over here.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.895
More garlic, the better.

00:07:23.895 --> 00:07:26.790
(food processor whirring)

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:31.173
This looks good to me.

00:07:32.461 --> 00:07:34.677
I was gonna say don't put your face in it

00:07:34.677 --> 00:07:36.960
and I just put my face in it.

00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:41.666
(suspenseful music)

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.168
- [Fry Guy] Lift up.

00:07:47.168 --> 00:07:50.168
(suspenseful music)

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.970
- Okay. Moment of truth.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.560
I'm about to bring Asia in,

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.690
but I just want to take a quick moment

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.010
to just really take it all in

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.710
'cause I really did just
make a giant egg roll.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:05.880
Look at this.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.463
This compared to this.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.020
Hopefully, she likes it.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.033
Asia, please come in.

00:08:15.984 --> 00:08:16.817
(Asia gasps)

00:08:16.817 --> 00:08:19.033
- Oh my God. (laughs)

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.240
What the heck?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.530
Oh my God this is huge.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:24.870
- The big giant egg
roll that you asked for.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.010
- How much does this weigh?

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.110
- It actually weighs 15 pounds.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:32.220
It is 16 inches long and 6 inches wide.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.053
You ready?

00:08:33.053 --> 00:08:35.530
(upbeat music)

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.020
Let's see.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:40.853
- Ooh.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:43.533
Oh my gosh.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.800
This is so heavy. You guys have no idea.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.153
Okay.
- I've never-

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.630
Cheers.
- [Asia] Cheers.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.860
- [Tway] Oh, you can dip first.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:53.693
- [Asia] Oh, thank you.

00:08:53.693 --> 00:08:54.870
- [Tway] Since you're the guest.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.151
- [Asia] Thank you so, oh my God.

00:08:56.151 --> 00:08:58.920
(both laughs)

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.570
- Okay.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.940
Spice warning it might be a little spicy.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.020
- Okay. Disclaimer you guys,

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.910
I have a very low spice tolerance.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.590
So we'll see.
- Okay, maybe bite over there

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:09.438
and then you can get a lick over here.

00:09:09.438 --> 00:09:11.370
- No, I'm just gonna go for it.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.230
- All right.
(Asia laughs)

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.703
I warned her.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.757
We got, we got that on camera, right?

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:19.030
- Okay, okay, okay.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:19.890
- Okay.
- Ready?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.067
- Yup.
- 1, 2, 3.

00:09:22.067 --> 00:09:25.067
(suspenseful music)

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.244
Honestly, this is really good.

00:09:30.244 --> 00:09:32.418
(both laughs)

00:09:32.418 --> 00:09:33.690
Mm.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.740
- Well, there you go.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.640
My giant egg roll was a success.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:39.900
- Oh, and the sauce is really good too.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:41.070
- [Tway] Really?
- It's not that spicy,

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:42.630
it's not too spicy.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:43.980
- Okay. We'll see about that.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.180
- [Asia] Okay.
- Just wait.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.014
I'm just kidding.
- I know.

00:09:46.014 --> 00:09:46.847
(both laughs)

00:09:46.847 --> 00:09:48.090
- In the comments below,

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:51.180
let me know what I should make big next.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.661
And I'll see you next time.

00:09:52.661 --> 00:09:57.661
(upbeat music)
(shutter clicking)

00:09:57.715 --> 00:09:58.548
(beep)

00:09:58.548 --> 00:10:00.330
- My hand is cramping
'cause this is so heavy.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.685
- Okay. Let's put this back down.

00:10:01.685 --> 00:10:04.268
(upbeat music)

